{"title":"Saturday assorted links","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/939344393/0/marginalrevolution~Saturday-assorted-links.html","date":1766822303000,"content":"<p>1. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/phl43/status/2004579757191499802\" target=\"_blank\">Some observations on immigration and wage effects</a>.  The spread of immigrants to incipient high-wage areas may be one rise why the geographic mobility of resident Americans has gone down.</p>\r\n<p>2. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/Valen10Francois/status/2004552929584582753\" target=\"_blank\">No good explanation for why more boys than girls are born after wars</a>.</p>\r\n<p>3. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://ericbudish.org/publication/online-event-tickets-workshop-thats-the-ticket-an-ftc-workshop-about-online-ticket-sales-starting-at-1730/\" target=\"_blank\">Slides on ticket resale, by Eric Budish</a>.</p>\r\n<p>4. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/sndurlauf/status/2004735377639186440\" target=\"_blank\">Steven Durlauf recommends five 2025 books in economics</a>.</p>\r\n<p>5. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.ft.com/content/9e75eeb8-b6e6-4a90-b015-2732fa9a8774?utm_social_handle_id=18949452&amp;utm_social_post_id=634331946\" target=\"_blank\">The ongoing rise of YouTube</a> (FT).  “The creator economy advertising market is expected to reach $37bn this year, up 26 per cent from a year ago, according to the estimates by the Interactive Advertising Bureau. The group expects the market to rise another 18 per cent in 2026.”</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/12/saturday-assorted-links-541.html\">Saturday assorted links</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/